<title>USA: Deutsche Telekom rockets in heavy N.Y. trade.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Telekom rockets in heavy N.Y. trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German telecommunications company Deutsche Telekom DT.N made a splashy Wall Street debut on Monday, opening at 22-1/8, up 3-15/64 as investors swarmed to buy the stock.</p>
<p>The company was the runaway volume leader with 5.7 million shares traded less than 20 minutes after the stock opened on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
